program Graphs.
note Reachability over edge(X, Y) facts (directed), computed by the kernel's Datalog.
note linked(X, Y) is the undirected view; cyclic(X) means X can reach itself.

rule reachable(X, Y) if edge(X, Y).
rule reachable(X, Z) if edge(X, Y) and reachable(Y, Z).
rule cyclic(X) if reachable(X, X).
rule linked(X, Y) if edge(X, Y).
rule linked(Y, X) if edge(X, Y).

test "a chain and a loop" do
  fact edge(a, b), edge(b, c), edge(c, a), edge(c, d).
  assert holds reachable(a, d).
  assert holds cyclic(b).
  assert not (holds reachable(d, a)).
  assert holds linked(d, c).
end.
